# R23 The Last Dinner (side quest): Marianna Grey lays the Green Queen's last supper. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ host
marianna_grey [neutral]: The inn's cellar stands open and the ovens are hot. Alda is gone, leaving me the keys, so I have laid a supper for whoever still hungers. Each soul at the board has a parting request. Will you sit and help me see them answered?
set wv_dinner_asked
quest the_last_dinner asked
-> host_menu

~ host_menu
* Take a bench at the long table -> table
* Ask what she means by a parting request -> what
* [if item:wv_last_letters and not flag.letter_marianna] Hand her Walder Pye's letter -> vigil/letters:to_marianna
* [ends:the_last_dinner] Tell her there is no time to eat -> cold
* Leave her to the ovens -> END

~ what
marianna_grey [sad]: My grandmother always said you feed the dying first and ask them questions second. Tonight the whole village is dying a little, so I reckon it is safer to ask first.
-> host_menu

~ table
Narrator: Paper lanterns sway above a trestle groan-heavy with roast and loaf, a harvest spread laid at the wrong end of the night. Around it sit the square's strangest stragglers, studying their plates so they need not study one another.
-> table_menu

~ table_menu
* [if flag.dinner_fed >= 3] Lift a cup and call it a proper supper -> toast
* [if not flag.dinner_quill] Take the seat beside Ambrose Quill -> quill
* [if not flag.dinner_pip] Take the seat beside Pip Oakum -> pip
* [if not flag.dinner_gaunt] Take the seat beside Sergeant Gaunt -> gaunt
* [if not flag.dinner_tamsin] Take the seat beside Tamsin Ledger -> tamsin
* [ends:the_last_dinner] Leave the supper to go cold -> cold
* Step away from the board for now -> END

~ quill
ambrose_quill [sad]: My petition is modest. Hear the whole of my elegy through to the closing stanza, and do not glance toward the door while I read. No one has managed both yet.
* [Insight DC 12] Guess how the final stanza turns -> quill_guess | quill_ask
* Invite him to read from the top -> quill_ask

~ quill_guess
Narrator: You sense he found a rhyme for "doom" that is neither "room" nor "tomb", and you give him a solemn nod. He weeps gratefully into his suet pudding.
set dinner_quill
set dinner_fed += 1
-> table_menu

~ quill_ask
Narrator: He declaims to the rafters. It starts as a passable dirge, turns into a thumping march by the third stanza, and by the sixth has every boot under the table keeping time.
set dinner_quill
set dinner_fed += 1
-> table_menu

~ pip
pip_oakum [smile]: I want a proper chair up by the grown-ups where the brown loaf sits. And I want you to tell me the one thing that scares you worst, for my collection.
* [Insight DC 12] See what the boy is truly asking -> pip_guess | pip_ask
* Name your sharpest fear for him -> pip_ask

~ pip_guess
Narrator: He is fishing for the nameless dread in the dark, to know he is not the only one carrying it. You offer him a smaller, honest terror instead, and he takes it with a magistrate's gravity.
set dinner_pip
set dinner_fed += 1
-> table_menu

~ pip_ask
Narrator: You speak the fear plain across the breadboard. He prints it in careful block letters upon a scrap of pasteboard, blows the ink dry, and tucks it into his waistcoat.
set dinner_pip
set dinner_fed += 1
-> table_menu

~ gaunt
sgt_gaunt [weary]: A minor tactical adjustment, if you please. Put me at the far head farthest from the door, in the tall-backed oak chair, and breathe not a word that I requested it.
* [Insight DC 12] Read the purpose of the tall chair -> gaunt_guess | gaunt_ask
* Show him to the far chair -> gaunt_ask

~ gaunt_guess
Narrator: The high wainscot keeps his neck out of the window draft while giving him a clear line on every bolt-hole. You pull the chair out without a word, and he grants you a brisk barracks nod.
set dinner_gaunt
set dinner_fed += 1
-> table_menu

~ gaunt_ask
Narrator: You settle him at the head of the board in the high-backed oak chair. He arranges his elbows like a gentleman in a theatre box who has already Memorized the exits.
set dinner_gaunt
set dinner_fed += 1
-> table_menu

~ tamsin
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: I require the minutes of this supper to be read aloud, unedited, before the dishes are cleared. There ought to be an attested record that we sat and ate.
* [Insight DC 12] Hear the wish beneath the clerk's rule -> tamsin_guess | tamsin_ask
* Promise to read the minutes aloud -> tamsin_ask

~ tamsin_guess
Narrator: A ledger is simply how she prays that someone will remember we were here. You give your word, and her nib scratches the promise into the margin, which makes it law.
set dinner_tamsin
set dinner_fed += 1
-> table_menu

~ tamsin_ask
Narrator: You give your word to read the roll. She enters the hour in neat black ink, pauses with the nib hovered, and adds a footnote: quorum present, and fed.
set dinner_tamsin
set dinner_fed += 1
-> table_menu

~ toast
marianna_grey [smile]: To the Green Queen, and to every soul who kept her company tonight. May our next supper fall at a kinder hour.
Narrator: Pewter and earthenware clink down the row. For the space of a long breath, nobody looks toward the northern hill.
quest the_last_dinner served
set dinner_resolved
heal 3d8 party
hit_dice restore 2 party
give wv_feast_bread
-> END

~ cold
marianna_grey [sad]: Then I shall banking-sheet the pans and keep them in the oven. Someone will want a warm bite before the end.
Narrator: The long board waits empty beneath the paper lanterns while the grease turns white on every trencher.
quest the_last_dinner cold
set dinner_resolved
-> END

~ after
if quest.the_last_dinner == served
marianna_grey [smile]: That was a good supper, the finest the Green Queen ever laid. Mind your step out there.
else
marianna_grey [sad]: The bricks in the oven hold their heat well enough. If you come back this way, there will be a plate waiting.
endif
-> END
